{"name":"Basil","hex":"#879f84","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Basil","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A male given name from Ancient Greek, in quiet but steady use in the UK."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Basil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Basil","blocks":[{"text":"Basil, also called great basil, is a culinary herb of the family Lamiaceae (mints). It is a tender plant and is used in cuisines worldwide. In Western cuisine, the generic term \"basil\" refers to the variety also known as Genovese basil or sweet basil. Basil is native to tropical and subtopical Asia and Australasia from India and Sri Lanka east to southeastern China, Taiwan, and south through Southeast Asia, the Philippines, New Guinea, to northern Australia. In temperate climates basil is treated as an annual plant, but it can be grown as a short-lived perennial or biennial in warmer horticultural zones with tropical or Mediterranean climates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Ocimum_basilicum_8zz.jpg/330px-Ocimum_basilicum_8zz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basil","wikidata":"Q38859"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Ocimum_basilicum_desiccated_5145~2016_01_03.JPG/500px-Ocimum_basilicum_desiccated_5145~2016_01_03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Ocimum_basilicum_desiccated_5145~2016_01_03.JPG/1280px-Ocimum_basilicum_desiccated_5145~2016_01_03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Ocimum_basilicum_desiccated_5145~2016_01_03.JPG/500px-Ocimum_basilicum_desiccated_5145~2016_01_03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Desiccated basil showing s